  "articleBody": "When you're installing porcelain tile, it's easy to make a few common blunders that can cause big headaches down the road. Let's talk about some of the big ones and how to steer clear of them. First up is poor surface preparation. Seriously, if your subfloor isn't clean, smooth, dry, and level, you're just asking for trouble. This often leads to cracks or lippage, where tiles aren't perfectly flush. Make sure that surface is dialed in! Another frequent mistake is picking the wrong adhesive or not letting it cure for long enough. You can't just set the tiles and immediately walk all over them; standard adhesives need about a day to set before foot traffic, and grout needs even longer before heavy use. Rushing this step is a recipe for bond failure. Then there's bad spacing and leveling. Skipping those spacers or not checking for an even surface will result in an unprofessional look and potential tripping hazards. And don't forget about expansion joints! These are super important for larger areas or outdoor installations to prevent cracking due to temperature changes. If you're feeling overwhelmed, or if your project involves a tricky subfloor or wet areas, bringing in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of grief and ensure a beautiful, lasting finish.",
